==English==

===Etymology===
From a later variant of {{m|en|tachy}}, {{m|en|techy}}, {{m|en|teachie}}, {{m|en|tetchy}}, simulating {{suffix|touch|y|lang=en}}. More at {{l|en|tetchy}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtʌtʃi/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-touchy.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
:* {{rhymes|ʌtʃi|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# {{lb|en|of a situation}} Extremely [[sensitive]] or [[volatile]]; easily [[disturbed]] to the point of becoming [[unstable]]; requiring [[caution]] or [[tactfulness]].
#: ''It is an extremely '''touchy''' situation, with everybody's patience wearing thin.''
# {{lb|en|of a person}} Easily [[offended]]; [[oversensitive]]; [[ticklish]].
#: ''He can be very '''touchy''' when you talk about his cat, so be as tactful as possible.''

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|touchy-feely}}<!-- Not properly derived, since “touchy” rarely means “one who touches”. -->

